  "disassembler": "GNU objdump 2.44, x86-64 Intel syntax, -D -b binary -m i386:x86-64 -M intel --insn-width=15",
  "capture": "Original perf task-clock windows. Matching W^X pages captured before and after the measured window are byte-identical. Published bodies are 4 KiB aligned; identify their prologues by six consecutive x86 ABI stores, validate operands/offsets. Decode each full hit body, trimming trap padding and nonexecutable compact exit tables after the common jitExitState return. All sampled generated addresses are instruction starts.",
  "definitions": {
    "operation": "Disjoint classification by sampled instruction. [rsp+disp] is a native stack operand. A lea computes an address. Memory class for ambiguous object/heap operations is other memory.",
    "stack_home": "The prologue identifies the six consecutive 8-byte input homes and therefore the boundary of the 16-byte SSA homes. Index k=0..5 is arguments, state, counter, data, environment, frame.",
    "emitter_sequence": "Disjoint classification by source-generated x64_backend sequences. Entry inputs, fresh/resume selector, home\u2194call-block live copies at CALL_SAVED (99 words), helper argument setup and reloads, call and epilogue include only the exact matched instructions. Other code may have related costs. Emitter sequence and instruction class overlap.",
    "named property or reference counting": "Requires full named own-slot tag/shape-cache guard or the exact heap-tag mask/range/branch followed by the recognized reference-count update. Other flavors of lookup are outside those bins.",
    "site decoding": "Join exact two-word CALL_SAVED copies to the matching resume selector and 64-bit CALL_SITE immediate (low 32 bits bytecode PC, high 32 call flags). A bytecode opcode/name requires a full exact machine body match to a uniquely identified recorded compilation. Normal call opcodes can dispatch native or bytecode targets.",
    "ABI audit": "Search each complete sampled body and cold exits for a read or address-take of each saved slot, correcting for the 160-byte register-dump stack in the common exit stub. The exit helper reads the distinct register dump and SSA/deopt homes. Bodies repeat between windows. A read on a cold path establishes a use in this implementation.",
    "time estimation": "Exclusive sampled user CPU allocated from /proc for each window. These are observed attributed times, not projected savings. Software sampling may skid, particularly at a return or branch target."
  },
